WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.867
Mark Zaid, I want

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.401
to ask

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.869
you about something that Lindsey

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.104
Graham, Senator Lindsey Graham,

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.538
who of course, has endorsed

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.240
Donald Trump, is a big supporter,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.275
very vocal supporter of Donald Trump

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.277
and also an attorney.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.579
He said the following.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.446
He said President

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.948
Trump will have his day in court,

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.516
but espionage charges

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.251
are absolutely ridiculous.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.886
Whether you like Trump or not.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.588
He did not commit espionage.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.922
He did not disseminate, leak

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.190
or provide information

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.025
to a foreign power

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.493
or news organizations

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.294
to damage this country.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.630
He is on a tear about this.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.032
I would not be surprised

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.199
if we saw him on the Senate floor

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.435
making these arguments

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.037
as an attorney

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.838
and an expert on national security.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.775
What do you think of this argument?

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.142
Sure.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.943
And congratulations on your new program.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.546
Thanks. What he said is ridiculous.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.548
It is so hypocritical

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.450
and politically frustrating

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:50.850
because that's

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.952
what this is, is a political statement

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:53.653
by him.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.988
Lindsey Graham knows full

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.322
well the Espionage Act,

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.090
which dates back

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.991
a century,

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:01.594
encompasses a whole host of provisions,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.496
one of which is spying

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.831
for a foreign power

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.866
like Aldrich Ames or Robert

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.002
Hanssen, who recently passed away

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.036
And ironically,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:10.637
we see this

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.971
both on the left

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.840
extremism side

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.842
in support of Julian Assange

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.343
and Ed Snowden,

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.779
where that side decries are.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.147
They've been prosecuted

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.183
or charged under the Espionage Act.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.384
This is an espionage.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.419
And yet now we see it on the right.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.755
It has nothing to do with espionage.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.157
In the formal James Bond sense,

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.026
other than the statute

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.394
is called the Espionage Act.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:38.131
This is, as is made clear in seven 93 E,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.332
which is the charge

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.668
he has been assessed with.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.370
It has to do with unlawful retention

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.872
of national defense information

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.207
and failing to return it.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.641
Lindsey Graham should know better.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:49.909
He does know better.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:53.580
Well, Andy, he is sticking by it.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.981
But I think that the point

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.682
that Marc just made

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:56.416
is really important

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.252
there is that the law and the statute

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.855
then there is also what it conjures up

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.389
when you hear espionage

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.791
and the politics of that

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.825
and push back

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.828
on the notion that espionage equals spy

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.497
and that he was somehow involved in

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.064
that kind of

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.066
and that kind of work

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.033
by the former president.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.535
The Conjuring creates

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.437
a great political opportunity for people

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.438
like Lindsey Graham,

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.973
but it has no legal significance.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.474
Mark is exactly right.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.576
The statute that the former president

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.811
charged under

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.881
is very well-suited for the behavior

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.349
that we now know he engaged in.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.484
I want to ask you about Hillary Clinton,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.319
your favorite topic.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.655
You were deputy FBI

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.757
director when there was an investigation

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.459
of her and her.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.060
Much talked about emails.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.029
I want you to listen to

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.365
the Republicans repeatedly

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.566
alluding to that.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.567
Talking about that

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.737
as they discuss the Trump case.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.472
I don't think there should be classified

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.474
documents at Mar a Lago.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.041
Joe Biden's

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.210
garage on Hillary Clinton's server.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.012
What he did is very similar,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.447
in my view, to what Hillary Clinton did.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.050
People in the Clinton case took a hammer

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.052
to a BlackBerry and destroyed it.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.787
You had Secretary Clinton

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.023
who had classified material on a server.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.090
She was not president

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:11.624
of the United States.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.092
She was Secretary Clinton.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.160
You have that happen.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.428
Nothing happens to her.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:17.864
You know the facts.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.299
What are the facts?

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:19.732
Well, then,

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.000
as you know, cases

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.835
come down to facts and evidence,

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.003
not politics.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.071
And these two cases

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.240
could not be more different on the facts.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:27.840
So let's talk

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.075
about what we actually found

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.944
in the Hillary Clinton email case.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:31.411
Yes.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.045
Hillary Clinton

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:32.912
maintained private

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.013
servers, emails went

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.315
across those servers.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.683
Ultimately, she returned

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.951
30,000 emails

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.586
to the Department of Defense work

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.987
related emails.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:41.854
In addition to those,

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:42.855
we found thousands

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:43.523
more emails

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.692
that she exchanged with people.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.660
The total

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.295
classified material

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.296
seized from

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.798
that review

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:54.701
were essentially 55 email conversation

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.735
strings of emails

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.570
in which eight were classified

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.706
top secret, 37 secret

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.140
and ten confidential.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.475
Now, it's important to remember

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.510
those weren't classified documents.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.179
That was simply the content

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.680
of email exchanges

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.450
that was later deemed to be classified

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.684
These weren't documents

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.487
with with classified stamping on the tops

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.555
and bottoms and cover sheets

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.689
and all that kind of stuff.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.690
Should it have happened?

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.660
No, but what we didn't have was evidence

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.761
that Hillary Clinton

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.396
had intentionally

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.231
exchanged or withheld

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.533
classified information.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.901
And that's just what we could

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:29.769
and could not prove.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.703
At the end of the day,

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:31.838
In the Trump case,

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:35.275
you have, what, 300 plus classified

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.609
documents, full documents

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.945
seized from his residence at Mar a Lago.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:39.779
Some of

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.781
most of which from the photographs

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.317
we've seen had headers and footers

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.719
that the proper stamping portion

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.087
markings on paragraphs,

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.389
cover sheets indicating

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.590
they were some of the most

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.358
classified materials we have.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:52.692
And then,

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.526
of course,

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.696
engaged in a long series of exchanges

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.298
and activity in an effort

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.300
to obstruct that investigation.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.968
Very, very different facts.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.036
Thank you for saying that.

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:04.470
Thank you for explaining that.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.507
What about ism is very intense right now.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.841
And you are

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.710
somebody who definitely knows facts

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.744
on this case.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:12.312
Thank you.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.379
Thank you very much, Mark

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.414
Zaid, appreciate it.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.815
I know, Jeff, you

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.984
you spent a lot of time last week in Iowa

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.819
you spent a lot of time

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.688
every year in Iowa.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.122
You've been in contact

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.357
with your sources back there.

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.224
What are you hearing from

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.959
Republicans in the first caucus state?

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.294
I was talking to a Republican who met

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.162
with the former president

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.963
when he was in Iowa just last week.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.032
And he said, look,

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.834
the wagons are being circled.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.469
Yes, Republicans are rallying behind him,

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.171
but there is still an opening

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.806
the same opening that existed last week.

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:40.773
And now there's more reason

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.607
for that opening.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:42.375
If there were

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.944
any Republicans who had pause about

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.646
can he be elected?

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.481
This is raising some concern.

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.082
But he said, look,

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.149
we're going to have to sit back

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.617
and watch it all.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.453
And the indictment has not been read

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:54.821
by most Republican voters.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:56.356
This happens to be a lawyer,

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.324
a Republican lawyer who met with him,

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:58.758
who said, look,

00:05:58.758 --> 00:05:59.659
I have read the indictment.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.627
He said it's pretty damning.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:02.995
His words echoed what

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.130
Bill Barr, the former attorney

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.366
general, said. This is not a witch hunt.

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.834
These are serious matters here.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.203
So I think the voters, the,

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.337
you know, the elite voters,

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.705
I guess perhaps the

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.841
the lawyers and others are studying this,

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:16.676
but we just have to give us some time.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:17.844
Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:19.679
Most people have not read the indictment,

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.647
which is why the former president

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.181
is trying

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.449
to put his stamp on it,

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.917
trying to fill that void.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:25.651
I mean, legally

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:26.586
is a whole different question,

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:28.054
which we'll talk about later.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:28.855
But when it comes

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:30.423
to the politics of this,

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.624
what he said on the campaign

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:32.825
trail is very telling

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:36.496
which

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:39.532
witch hunt, scam, hoax?

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:42.301
It's called election interference.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.403
And they're doing the best

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:44.504
they can with it.

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.305
The baseless indictment of me

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:49.041
by the Biden administration's weaponized

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:52.078
Department of Injustice

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:52.845
will go down

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:53.346
as among

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:55.481
the most horrific abuses of power

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:57.683
in the history of our country.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.552
As far as the

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.953
joke of an indictment,

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.455
it's a horrible thing.

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:04.857
It's a horrible thing for this country.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:07.760
Witch hunt, witch hunt, scam, hoax.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.362
It's like it's like the greatest hits.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.731
He's the king of the buzz word.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.199
And it works.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:14.434
It is very effective.

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.735
I mean, repetition has always been

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:16.436
one of Trump's

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:18.604
most important tools in his toolkit.

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.673
But I think that the Republican Party

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.274
is grappling

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.542
with some structural issues

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:23.676
here, namely,

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.344
that the Republican Party,

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:25.878
as exists

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:26.512
here, was

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.147
was formed and structured

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.882
by Trump himself.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.717
He popularized lock

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.953
her up, made Hillary Clinton's

00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:35.488
email issue

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:37.323
one of the foundational

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:39.425
rallying cries of the Republican Party.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:41.394
And so it's for that reason.

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:42.195
You know what I hear

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:43.262
from a lot of Republicans

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.631
is that if only for that one reason,

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:46.666
many of them

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:47.800
can't see a world

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.835
in which they say

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:50.603
that Trump should be charged

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:52.572
for a document

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:54.640
classified document related issue

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.309
when Hillary Clinton was not.

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:57.176
The logic of it,

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.311
if you've read the indictment,

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.345
if you look at the evidence,

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:01.080
does not make any sense.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.782
But that is part of the

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:03.483
you know,

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:03.883
that's part

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:04.383
of the

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.185
the DNA of the Republican Party

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.119
right now.

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.788
And many of these candidates, that's

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:10.089
why you're seeing so many of them,

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:11.491
even the ones who are criticizing

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:12.825
Trump, like Chris Christie,

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.094
they can't do it without saying, well,

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:15.828
Hillary Clinton

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:17.930
should have been charged, but

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.098
it's always the butt

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.266
that gets in the way.

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.634
And they're really trying

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:23.803
to conflate the two situations,

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:25.371
although their cases are

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:26.405
dramatically different.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:26.905
I mean,

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.274
really what this indictment shows

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:29.308
is Trump's effort

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.377
to try to allegedly cover up

00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:32.512
these documents

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:33.613
that are trying to be retrieved

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:34.881
by the federal government

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:35.314
is effort

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.415
to try to hide them,

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:38.284
the misstatements that he allegedly made

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:38.985
all about it.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:39.652
That is not

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.420
what it's not about simply

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.256
mishandling classified documents,

00:08:43.256 --> 00:08:44.757
which is what the Biden situation was,

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:45.124
what the Penn

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.092
situation was,

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.628
what Hillary Clinton situation was after.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.763
You know, we learned that Pence

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:53.032
cooperated, that case has been closed,

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:54.634
providing the documents back to them.

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:56.235
Biden apparently is cooperating.

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.003
We don't know exactly

00:08:57.003 --> 00:08:58.137
what's going to happen,

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.005
that investigation,

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:01.140
but these are much different cases.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.241
But the argument,

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.477
the political argument, facts be damned.

00:09:04.477 --> 00:09:05.444
They're going to make that case

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:07.313
to try to suggest one of the same.

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:08.180
The big question, too,

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:08.981
for a lot of Republicans

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.883
is how quickly does this happen?

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:12.518
Does this drag for the election year

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:14.820
or does it is a punted until 20, 25?

